# Seeded tiers

Generated by `make generate` from [`docs/data/features.json`](../data/features.json) and [`capabilities.json`](../data/capabilities.json); not edited by hand.
The [capability roadmap](capability-roadmap.md) explains how to read it.

## Features by lowest seeded tier

A feature is in its lowest seeded tier and every tier above it.

| Feature | Kind | Gates | Free | Starter | Business | Enterprise | Phase |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `stacks` | capability | The Stacks tag | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | P5 |
| `aggregated` | option | `vcsChecks: AGGREGATED` | | | ✓ | ✓ | P12 |
| `audit-trail` | capability | The [Audit](../research/a.md#x) tag \| more | | | | ✓ | P18b |

## Seeded limits

Every limit is pooled across an organization's accounts. An empty cell means no limit.

| Limit | Unit | Free | Starter | Business | Enterprise | Phase |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `seats` | members, [see](https://example.com/x) | 2 | 2 | | | P3b |

## Summary by phase

Counts of the reference rows each phase owns. Superseded counts the rows no phase builds.

| Phase | Tags | Resources (API) | Data sources (API) | `BillingTierFeature` values |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| P3 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0 |
| P3b | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| P5 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1 |
| P10 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| Superseded | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 |
| Total | 3 | 2 | 1 | 1 |
